# Resume rules

- Preserve factual accuracy. Never invent tools, ownership, scale, users, publications, employment, or metrics.
- Layers are evidence bank, two-page master (inventory), frozen family
  one-pagers from BUILD, then Polar ROUTE. VIP tailor is optional.
- Do not restore `scripts/build_clusters.py`. Historical cluster files are
  benchmark artifacts only.
- Regular rows attach a resume already on the widget, or upload
  `resumes/Perfect Resume/perfect_resume.pdf` when a file must be ingested.
  Do not upload the two-page master. Do not generate a resume from a JD
  at apply time. Do not guess among family variants.
- VIP / exceptional prioritized rows may run
  `scripts/resume_quality.py run --jd` from the evidence bank only.
- Prioritize demonstrated outcomes and technical decisions over keyword stuffing.
- Reuse the employer's terminology only when it accurately describes existing experience.
- Keep bullets concise and interview-defensible.
- Flag missing evidence instead of manufacturing it.
- When recommending a change, identify the target job requirement and the supporting user evidence.
